14. Separate Jules tasks and acceptance criteria
Task A --- Audit (P0)
- Three audit documents produced; no functional changes.
- Firebase IDs compared across client, rules and Functions.
- Tests run or explicitly marked not runnable.
- Audio, claims, subscription and privacy risks evidenced.
- No production data/configuration changed.
Task B --- Core player (P0/P1)
- Deterministic play/pause/stop transitions.
- Repeated taps do not create multiple streams.
- Timer/fade and interruption behaviour verified.
- UI does not falsely show playing after an error.
- Regression suite and device matrix completed.
- No entitlement/Firebase regressions.
Task C --- Content integrity (P1)
- Exact claims inventoried.
- High-risk claims corrected or escalated for owner review.
- Frequency tradition distinguished from established science.
- Low-frequency/binaural explanations technically accurate.
- Research sources and review dates included; no invented citations.
Task D --- Intention-first discovery (P1)
- Users can start from intention or browse frequencies.
- No mandatory long onboarding.
- Cards accurately represent actual session behaviour.
- Experiment has primary metric and guardrails.
- Favourites, deep links and admin content remain functional.
Task E --- Affirmation audio proof of concept (P1/P2)
- One primary sound plus one spoken source tested on supported
  iOS/Android.
- Speech can be disabled without unexpectedly stopping the primary
  sound.
- No duplicate streams; volume/ducking documented.
- Interruption, lock/background and headphone behaviour recorded.
- Optional feature with sound-only mode.
Task F --- Analytics (P1/P2)
- Each event supports a defined decision.
- No sensitive free text logged.
- Purchase events rely on provider-confirmed state.
- Collection/retention documented.
- Analytics failure does not block playback.
Task G --- Monetisation/release (P1)
- Restore purchases tested.
- Provider-confirmed entitlement updates verified.
- Cancellation, expiry, refund/revocation paths tested or marked as
  gaps.
- Client cannot grant itself premium.
